        <initializer>= 0x43FFu</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>POR value per datasheet Rev 1.2 §5.3.3.6 p.89: LIM_VALUE_ABS = 0x3FF (1023, the field maximum) and AUTO_LIM_VALUE_ABS = 0x10 (16). This register was previously documented here as resetting to 0x0000, which would have meant a zero integrator clamp and an Autolimit threshold violating the §4.6.2.3 constraint. It does not: the reset state already satisfies AUTO_LIM_VALUE_ABS &gt; MIN_INT_THRESH+3 while MIN_INT_THRESH is at its own reset value of 0, so leaving this register unwritten is safe. Anything doing a read-modify-write against the old 0x0000 assumption would have silently destroyed both clamps. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
